    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">This is not a book about how to organize or declutter, nor is it one that promotes minimalism. Instead, it invites us to reexamine our relationship with the things we own and reawaken the long-forgotten joy in the beauty of everyday life. Through a life that intentionally adds—not reduces—objects, Fujioka Minami reaffirms the core values that shape how she wants to live the rest of her life. Life, self, and time are inseparable. If you feel stuck in routine or have lost your sense of direction, give this approach a try—you just might discover something truly meaningful</marc:subfield>
